<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Province of New Jersey</h1><p class="st-meta">1664 CE – 1776 CE · capital Perth Amboy</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The English colony between the Hudson and Delaware rivers, granted in 1664, split in two for a generation and reunited under the Crown in 1702.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After seizing <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-netherland">New Netherland</a> in 1664, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-england">James, Duke of York</a>, granted the land between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-river">Hudson</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delaware-river">Delaware</a> to Lord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-berkeley-1st-baron-berkeley-of-stratton">John Berkeley</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-carteret">Sir George Carteret</a>, naming it after Carteret's home island of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bailiwick-of-jersey">Jersey</a>. Their Concession and Agreement of 1665 promised religious freedom and an elected assembly, drawing settlers to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-new-jersey">Elizabethtown</a> and other towns.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Disputes over land and quitrents led to division into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/east-jersey">East Jersey</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/west-jersey">West Jersey</a>, which existed from 1674 until the proprietors surrendered government to the Crown in 1702. The reunited royal colony shared its governor with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-new-york">Province of New York</a> until 1738, and its capital alternated between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perth-amboy">Perth Amboy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burlington-new-jersey">Burlington</a>. Diverse Puritan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quakers">Quaker</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> and Scottish settlers farmed grain, and the colleges that became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princeton-university">Princeton</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rutgers-university">Rutgers</a> were founded in 1746 and 1766.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Royal governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-franklin">William Franklin</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benjamin-franklin">Benjamin Franklin</a>, was arrested in 1776. On 2 July 1776 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a> adopted a state constitution, and it became a state of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/province-of-new-jersey.jpg" alt="Province of New Jersey" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: AnonMoos, based on image by Zscout370, AnonMoos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Red_ensign_of_Great_Britain_(1707%E2%80%931800,_square_canton).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1664 CE – 1776 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Perth Amboy</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>George Carteret, Lewis Morris, William Franklin</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestantism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>New Jersey (colony)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1720&amp;focus=province-of-new-jersey" aria-label="Province of New Jersey on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2855 721 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Province of New Jersey lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3175 977L4970 663M3175 977L4997 651M3175 977L2570 1008M3175 977L3177 986M3175 977L3174 997"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4970 663h0M4997 651h0M2570 1008h0M3177 986h0M3174 997h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3175 977h0"/><path class